4005:
**πεντηκοστός**, -ή, -όν 
[in LXX for חֲמִישִׁי, חֲמִישִׁי, [[03-leviticus.25.10|Lev.25:10-11]], [[12-2-kings.15.23|4Ki.15:23 15:27]]; 1Ma.4:1-61, 2Ma.14:4; ἡ π., Tob.2:1, 2Ma.12:32 * ;] 
fiftieth. As subst., ἡ π.; 
(a) (sc. μερίς), at Athens, a tax of two per cent.; 
(b) (sc. ἡμέρα, i.e. the fiftieth day after the Passover), Pentecost, the second of the three great Jewish feasts (To, 2Mac, ll. with; ἑορτὴ ἑβδομάδων, [[05-deuteronomy.16.10|Deu.16:10]], al.) : [[44-acts.2.1|Act.2:1 20:16]], [[46-1-corinthians.16.8|1Co.16:8]].
(AS)

4009:
**πέρας**, -ατος, τό
(πέρα, beyond), [in LXX chiefly for קֵץ, קָצָה and cognate forms ;] 
**an end, limit, boundary**; 
(a) **of space**: chiefly in pl., τὰ π. τ. γῆς, [[40-matthew.12.42|Mat.12:42]], [[42-luke.11.31|Luk.11:31]]; τ. οἰκουμένης, [[45-romans.10.18|Rom.10:18]] (LXX); 
(b) (opposite to ἀρχή) the end: with genitive, ἀντιλογίας, [[58-hebrews.6.10|Heb.6:10.]]
(AS)

4016:
**περι-βάλλω **
[in LXX chiefly for כָּסָה pi., also for לָבַשׁ, עָטָה, etc. ;] 
**to throw around or over, put on or over**; 
(a) **of siege or defen­sive works**: χάρακά σοι, [[42-luke.19.43|Luk.19:43]] (WH, mg.; παρεμβ-, WH, txt.); 
(b) **of clothing, to put on, wrap about, clothe with**: with accusative of thing(s), [[42-luke.23.11|Luk.23:11;]] with accusative of person(s), [[40-matthew.25.36|Mat.25:36, 38 25:43]]; with dupl. accusative (not cl.; Bl., § 34, 4), [[43-john.19.2|Jhn.19:2;]] pf. pass., **to have wrapped round one**: with accusative of thing(s) (cl.), [[41-mark.14.51|Mrk.14:51 16:5]], [[66-revelation.7.9|Rev.7:9, 13 10:1 11:3 12:1 17:4 18:16 19:13]]; with dative of thing(s), [[66-revelation.4.4|Rev.4:4]] (WH, txt.; before ἐν, WH, mg.); fut., before ἐν (of. [[05-deuteronomy.22.12|Deu.22:12]], [[19-psalms.45.9|Psa.45:9, 13]]), [[66-revelation.3.5|Rev.3:5]]. Mid., **to clothe oneself, wrap round or put on oneself**: absol., [[40-matthew.6.29|Mat.6:29]], [[42-luke.12.27|Luk.12:27]], [[66-revelation.3.18|Rev.3:18]]; with accusative of thing(s), [[40-matthew.6.31|Mat.6:31]], [[44-acts.12.8|Act.12:8]], [[66-revelation.19.8|Rev.19:8]].
(AS)

4088:
**πικρία**, -ας, ἡ
(πικρός), [in LXX chiefly for מַר and cognate forms ;] 
**bitterness**; 
(a) of taste (Arist., [[24-jeremiah.15.17|Jer.15:17]], al.); 
(b) metaphorically, of temper, character, etc.: [[45-romans.3.14|Rom.3:14]] (LXX), [[49-ephesians.4.31|Eph.4:31;]] ῥίζα πικρίας, [[58-hebrews.12.15|Heb.12:15;]] χολὴ π., a malignant disposition, [[44-acts.8.23|Act.8:23.]]
(AS)

4094:
**πίναξ**, -ακος, ὁ 
[in LXX: 4Ma.17:7 R * ;] 
prop., a board, plank; hence, of various at wooden articles; 
(a) **a tablet**; 
(b) **a disc, a dish**: [[40-matthew.14.8|Mat.14:8, 11]], [[41-mark.6.25|Mrk.6:25, 28]] [[42-luke.11.39|Luk.11:39]].
(AS)

4137:
**πληρόω**, -ῶ 
[in LXX chiefly for מָלֵא ;] 
1. to fill, make full, fill to the full, with accusative; 
(a) **of things **: pass. (σαψήνη, φάραγξ), [[40-matthew.13.48|Mat.13:48]], [[42-luke.3.5|Luk.3:5]]" (LXX) ; figuratively, [[40-matthew.23.32|Mat.23:32;]] but chiefly of immaterial things: πᾶσαν χρείαν, [[50-philippians.4.19|Php.4:19;]] ἦχος ἐλήρωσε τ. οἶκον, [[44-acts.2.2|Act.2:2;]] with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), [[44-acts.5.28|Act.5:28;]] pass., before ἐκ, [[43-john.12.3|Jhn.12:3]] (cf. B1., § 36, 4); π. τ. καρδίαν, [[43-john.16.6|Jhn.16:6]], [[44-acts.5.3|Act.5:3]]; metaphorically, of the all-pervading activity of Christ, [[49-ephesians.4.10|Eph.4:10;]] mid., [[49-ephesians.1.23|Eph.1:23;]] 
(b) **of persons**: to fill with, **cause to abound in **: with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), [[44-acts.2.28|Act.2:28]] (LXX), [[45-romans.15.13|Rom.15:13;]] pass., **to be filled with, abound in**: [[49-ephesians.3.19|Eph.3:19]], [[50-philippians.4.18|Php.4:18]]; with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), [[44-acts.13.52|Act.13:52]], [[45-romans.15.14|Rom.15:14]], [[55-2-timothy.1.4|2Ti.1:4]]; with dative (Æsch., al.), [[42-luke.2.40|Luk.2:40]] (with genitive, T), [[45-romans.1.29|Rom.1:29]], [[47-2-corinthians.7.4|2Co.7:4]]; with accusative (so in π., see MM, xx), [[50-philippians.1.11|Php.1:11]], [[51-colossians.1.9|Col.1:9]]; before ἐν, [[49-ephesians.5.18|Eph.5:18]], [[51-colossians.2.10|Col.2:10]]. 
2. **to complete**; 
(a) **to complete, fulfil**: of number, [[66-revelation.6.11|Rev.6:11]], WH, tat.; of time (MM, xx), [[41-mark.1.15|Mrk.1:15]], [[42-luke.21.24|Luk.21:24]], [[43-john.7.8|Jhn.7:8]], [[44-acts.7.23|Act.7:23, 30 9:23 24:27]]; ἐυδοκίαν, [[53-2-thessalonians.1.11|2Th.1:11;]] τ. χαράν, [[50-philippians.2.2|Php.2:2;]] pass., [[43-john.3.29|Jhn.3:29 15:11 16:24 17:13]], [[62-1-john.1.4|1Jn.1:4]], [[63-2-john.12.1|2Jn.12]]; τ. ἔργα, [[66-revelation.3.2|Rev.3:2;]] ἡ ὑπακυή, [[47-2-corinthians.10.6|2Co.10:6;]] τ. πάσχα, [[42-luke.22.16|Luk.22:16;]] 
(b) **to execute, accomplish, carry out to the full**: [[40-matthew.3.15|Mat.3:15]], [[42-luke.7.1|Luk.7:1 9:31]], [[44-acts.12.25|Act.12:25 13:25 14:26 19:21]], [[45-romans.8.4|Rom.8:4 13:8 15:19]], [[48-galatians.5.14|Gal.5:14]], [[51-colossians.1.25|Col.1:25 4:17]], [[66-revelation.6.11|Rev.6:11]], T, WH, R, mg.; 
(with) of sayings, prophecies, etc., **to bring to pass, fulfil**: [[40-matthew.1.22|Mat.1:22 2:15, 17 2:23 4:14 5:17 8:17 12:17 13:35 21:4 26:54, 56 27:9]], [[41-mark.14.49|Mrk.14:49 15:28]] (WH, R, txt. om.), [[42-luke.1.20|Luk.1:20 4:21 24:44]], [[43-john.12.38|Jhn.12:38 13:18 15:25 17:12 18:9, 32 19:24, 36]], [[44-acts.1.16|Act.1:16 3:18 13:27]], [[59-james.2.23|Jas.2:23]] (cf. Lft., Col., 255 ff.).
(AS)

4152:
**πνευματικός**, -ή, -όν
(πνεῦμα), 
1. of or caused by the wind, air or breath (Arist., al.). 
2. **spiritual **(opposite to σωματικός, Plut.); 
(a) **of created beings **: τὰ π. (RV, the spiritual hosts), [[49-ephesians.6.12|Eph.6:12;]] of that which is related to the human spirit, opposite to ψυχικός, [[46-1-corinthians.15.44|1Co.15:44 15:46]]; 
(b) **of that which belongs to or is actuated by the Divine Spirit**; 
α **of persons **: [[46-1-corinthians.2.15|1Co.2:15 3:1 14:37]], [[48-galatians.6.1|Gal.6:1]]; οἶκος π., figuratively, [[60-1-peter.2.5|1Pe.2:5;]] 
β **of things **: [[45-romans.1.11|Rom.1:11 7:14]], [[46-1-corinthians.2.13|1Co.2:13 10:3-4 12:1 14:1]], [[49-ephesians.1.3|Eph.1:3 5:19]], [[51-colossians.1.9|Col.1:9 3:16]], [[60-1-peter.2.5|1Pe.2:5]]; opposite to τ. σαρκικά, [[45-romans.15.27|Rom.15:27]], [[46-1-corinthians.9.11|1Co.9:11]].
_SYN._: ψυχικός, which see, and cf. _DB_, ii, 410, iv, 612 (AS)

4314:
**πρός**, 
_prep. with genitive, dative, accusative_ 
I. I. C. genitive, of motion from a place, **from the side of**, hence metaphorically, **in the interests of**, [[44-acts.27.34|Act.27:34]] (cf. Page, in l.). 
II. II. C. dative, of local proximity, **hard by, near, at**: [[41-mark.5.11|Mrk.5:11]], [[42-luke.19.37|Luk.19:37]], [[43-john.18.16|Jhn.18:16 20:11, 12]] [[66-revelation.1.13|Rev.1:13]]. 
III. C. accusative, of motion or direction towards a place or object, **to, towards**. 
1. Of place, 
(a) **after verbs of motion or of speaking and other words with the idea of direction**: ἔρχομαι, ἀναβαίνω, πορεύομαι, λέγω, ἐπιστολή, etc., [[40-matthew.3.14|Mat.3:14]], [[41-mark.6.51|Mrk.6:51]], [[42-luke.11.5|Luk.11:5]], [[43-john.2.3|Jhn.2:3]], [[44-acts.9.2|Act.9:2]], al. mult.; metaphorically, of mental direction, hostile or otherwise, [[42-luke.23.12|Luk.23:12]], [[43-john.6.52|Jhn.6:52]], [[47-2-corinthians.7.4|2Co.7:4]], [[49-ephesians.6.12|Eph.6:12]], [[51-colossians.3.13|Col.3:13]], al.; of the issue or end, [[42-luke.14.32|Luk.14:32]], [[43-john.11.4|Jhn.11:4]], al.; of purpose, [[40-matthew.26.12|Mat.26:12]], [[45-romans.3.26|Rom.3:26]], [[46-1-corinthians.6.5|1Co.6:5]], al.; πρὸς τό, with inf., denoting purpose (cf. M, _Pr._, 218, 220; Lft., _Notes_, 131), [[40-matthew.5.28|Mat.5:28]], [[41-mark.13.22|Mrk.13:22]], [[49-ephesians.6.11|Eph.6:11]], [[52-1-thessalonians.2.9|1Th.2:9]], al.; 
(b) of close proximity, **at, by, with**: [[40-matthew.3.10|Mat.3:10]], [[41-mark.11.4|Mrk.11:4]], [[42-luke.4.11|Luk.4:11]], [[44-acts.3.2|Act.3:2]], al.; after εἶναι, [[40-matthew.13.56|Mat.13:56]], [[41-mark.6.3|Mrk.6:3]], [[43-john.1.1|Jhn.1:1]], al.
2. 2. Of time, 
(a) **towards** (Plat., Xen., LXX: [[01-genesis.8.11|Gen.8:11]], al.): [[42-luke.24.29|Luk.24:29]]; 
(b) **for**: πρὸς καιρόν, [[42-luke.8.13|Luk.8:13]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.5|1Co.7:5]]; πρὸς ὥραν, [[43-john.5.35|Jhn.5:35]], al.; πρὸς ὀλίγον, [[59-james.4.14|Jas.4:14.]] 
3. Of relation 
(a) **toward, with**: [[45-romans.5.1|Rom.5:1]], [[47-2-corinthians.1.12|2Co.1:12]], [[51-colossians.4.5|Col.4:5]], [[52-1-thessalonians.4.12|1Th.4:12]], al.; 
(b) **with regard to**: [[40-matthew.19.8|Mat.19:8]], [[41-mark.12.12|Mrk.12:12]], [[45-romans.8.31|Rom.8:31]], al.; 
(with) **pertaining to, to**: [[40-matthew.27.4|Mat.27:4]], [[43-john.21.22|Jhn.21:22]], [[45-romans.15.17|Rom.15:17]], [[58-hebrews.2.17|Heb.2:17 5:1]]; 
(d) **according to**: [[42-luke.12.47|Luk.12:47]], [[47-2-corinthians.5.10|2Co.5:10]], [[48-galatians.2.14|Gal.2:14]], [[49-ephesians.3.4|Eph.3:4 4:14]]; 
(e) **in comparison with**: [[45-romans.8.18|Rom.8:18.]] 
IV. **In composition**: **towards** (προσέρχομαι), **to** (προσάγω), **against** (προσκόπτω), **besides** (προσδαπανάω) . 
(AS)

4352:
**προσ-κυνέω**, -ῶ
(κυνέω, to kiss), [in LXX chiefly for שָׁחָה hith. ;] 
**to make obeisance, do reverence to, worship**; 
(a) prop. (as in cl., of the gods: Hdt., Æsch., Plat., al.), of God, **Christ and supra-mundane beings**: absol., [[43-john.4.20|Jhn.4:20 12:20]], [[44-acts.8.27|Act.8:27 24:11]], [[58-hebrews.11.21|Heb.11:21]] (Westc., in l), [[66-revelation.11.1|Rev.11:1;]] πίπτειν καὶ π., [[66-revelation.5.14|Rev.5:14;]] with dative (of the significance of this constr. as com­pared with the usual cl., with accusative, see Abbott, _JG_, 78 f.; _JV_, 133 ff.), [[43-john.4.21|Jhn.4:21, 23]], [[44-acts.7.43|Act.7:43]], [[46-1-corinthians.14.25|1Co.14:25]], [[58-hebrews.1.6|Heb.1:6]], [[66-revelation.4.10|Rev.4:10 7:11 11:16 13:4, 15 14:7 16:2 19:4, 10 19:20 22:8-9]]; with accusative (see supr.), [[40-matthew.4.10|Mat.4:10]], [[42-luke.4.8|Luk.4:8 24:52]] (WH, R, mg., om.), [[43-john.4.22|Jhn.4:22, 24]], [[66-revelation.9.20|Rev.9:20 13:4, 8 13:12 14:9, 11 20:4]]; Seq. ἐπώπιον, [[42-luke.4.7|Luk.4:7]], [[66-revelation.15.4|Rev.15:4]]; 
(b) as in cl., of homage to human superiors (cf. MM, xxi): absol., [[40-matthew.20.20|Mat.20:20]], [[44-acts.10.25|Act.10:25]]; with dative (see supr.), [[40-matthew.2.2|Mat.2:2, 8 8:2 9:18 14:33 15:25 18:26 28:9]], [[41-mark.15.19|Mrk.15:19]], [[43-john.9.38|Jhn.9:38]]; πεσὼν., [[40-matthew.2.11|Mat.2:11 4:9]]; ἐνώπιον τ. ποδῶν, [[66-revelation.3.9|Rev.3:9;]] with accusative, [[41-mark.5.6|Mrk.5:6]] (dative T).
(AS)

4366:
**προσ-ρήγνυμι **
[in Aq.: [[19-psalms.2.9|Psa.2:9]] * ;] 
**to break against, dash against**; 
(a) trans. (παιδία πέτραις, FlJ, _Ant._, ix, 4, 6); 
(b) intrans., with dative: [[42-luke.6.48|Luk.6:48-49]] (cf. προσπίπτω).
(AS)

4396:
**προφήτης**, -ου, ὁ [πρόφημι, **to speak forth**), 
[in LXX chiefly for נָבִיא ;] 
one who acts as an interpreter or forth-teller of the Divine will (see Lft., _Notes_, 83f.; Tr., _Syn._, §vi), **a prophet**; 
1. in cl. (Æsch., Hdt., Plat., al.), of the interpreters of oracles. 
2. In NT, 
(a) **of the OT prophets**: [[40-matthew.5.12|Mat.5:12]], [[41-mark.6.15|Mrk.6:15]], [[42-luke.4.27|Luk.4:27]], [[43-john.8.52|Jhn.8:52]], [[45-romans.11.3|Rom.11:3]], al.; 
(b) **of prophets in general**: [[40-matthew.10.41|Mat.10:41 13:57 21:46]], [[41-mark.6.4|Mrk.6:4]], [[42-luke.13.33|Luk.13:33]], al.; 
(with) **of John the Baptist**: [[40-matthew.21.26|Mat.21:26]], [[41-mark.6.15|Mrk.6:15]], [[42-luke.1.76|Luk.1:76]]; 
(d) **of Christ**: [[40-matthew.21.11|Mat.21:11]], [[43-john.6.14|Jhn.6:14]], [[44-acts.3.22|Act.3:22, 23 7:37]]" (LXX) ; 
(e) **of Christian prophets in the apostolic age**: [[44-acts.15.32|Act.15:32]], [[46-1-corinthians.12.28|1Co.12:28]], [[49-ephesians.2.20|Eph.2:20]], al.; 
(f) by meton., of the writings of prophets: [[42-luke.24.27|Luk.24:27]], [[44-acts.8.28|Act.8:28]], al.; 
(g) **of a poet**: [[56-titus.1.12|Tit.1:12]] (on the use of the term in π. and Inscr., see Deiss., _BS_, 235f.; MM, xxii). 
(AS)

4465:
**ῥαβδοῦχος**, -ου, ό
(ῥαβδος, ἔχω), 
**one who carries a rod or staff of office**; 
(a) **an umpire or judge **(Plat.); 
(b) **in late writers, a Roman lictor**: [[44-acts.16.38|Act.16:38.]]
(AS)

4521:
**σάββατον**, -ου, τό (Aram. שַׁבָּתָא, transliterated σάββατα, and this being mistaken for a pl., the sing. σάββατον was formed from it), and σάββατα, -ων, τά 
[in LXX for שַׁבָּת, שַׁבָּתוֹן ;] 
1. the seventh day of the week, the sabbath 
(a) the sing. form -ον, τὸ σ.: [[40-matthew.12.8|Mat.12:8]], [[41-mark.2.27|Mrk.2:27]], [[42-luke.6.5|Luk.6:5]], al.; ἡ ἡμέρα τοῦ σ. (in LXX, [[02-exodus.20.8|Exo.20:8]], al., usually τῶν σ., see infr.), [[42-luke.13.16|Luk.13:16 14:5]]; ὁδὸς σαββάτου, [[44-acts.1.12|Act.1:12]] (cf. [[40-matthew.24.29|Mat.24:29]]); dative, of time (τῷ) σ., [[42-luke.6.9|Luk.6:9 14:1]]; ἐν (τῷ) σ., [[40-matthew.12.2|Mat.12:2]], [[42-luke.6.7|Luk.6:7]], [[43-john.5.16|Jhn.5:16]], al.; accusative, of duration, τὸ σ., [[42-luke.23.56|Luk.23:56;]] κατὰ πᾶν σ., [[44-acts.13.27|Act.13:27 15:21 18:4]]; pl., σ. τρία, [[44-acts.17.2|Act.17:2]] R, txt. (but see infr.); 
(b) as most frequently in LXX (see Swete, _Mk._, 17; Thackeray, _Gr._, 35) the pl. form, τὰ σ. (see supr. on the Aram. form. There is also an analogy in the names of other festivals, τ. ἐγκαίνια, ἄζυμα, etc.): [[40-matthew.28.1|Mat.28:1]], [[51-colossians.2.16|Col.2:16]]; ἡ ἡμέρα τῶν σ. ([[02-exodus.20.8|Exo.20:8]], al.), [[42-luke.4.16|Luk.4:16]], [[44-acts.13.14|Act.13:14 16:13]]; dative pl. (in LXX -τοις, but 1Ma.2:38 as in NT) by metaplasmus (El., § 9, 3), σάββασι, [[40-matthew.12.1|Mat.12:1, 5 12:10-12]] [[41-mark.1.21|Mrk.1:21 2:23 3:2, 4]], [[42-luke.4.31|Luk.4:31 6:2]]. 
2. **seven days, a week**; 
(a) the sing. form: πρώτη σαββάτσυ, [[41-mark.16.9|Mrk.16:9;]] δὶς τοῦ σ. (Bl., § 35, 4; 36, 13), [[42-luke.18.12|Luk.18:12;]] κατὰ μίαν σαββάτου, [[46-1-corinthians.16.2|1Co.16:2;]] pl., σ. τρία, [[44-acts.17.2|Act.17:2]] R, mg. (but see supr.); 
(b) the pl. form: ἡ μία τῶν σ. (where the genitive = μετὰ τά; Soph., _Lex._, 43a), [[40-matthew.28.1|Mat.28:1]], [[41-mark.16.2|Mrk.16:2]], [[42-luke.24.1|Luk.24:1]], [[43-john.20.1|Jhn.20:1, 19]], [[44-acts.20.7|Act.20:7]] 
(AS)

4540:
**Σαμαρία** (Rec. -άρεια), -ας, ἡ (Heb. שֹׁמְרוֹן; Aram. שָׁמְרַיִן), 
**Samaria**; 
(a) **the city**: [[44-acts.8.5|Act.8:5]] (and perhaps also [[44-acts.8.9|Act.8:9, 14]]); 
(b) **the region**: [[42-luke.17.11|Luk.17:11]], [[43-john.4.4|Jhn.4:4-5]], 7, [[44-acts.1.8|Act.1:8 8:1]] (and perhaps also [[44-acts.8.9|Act.8:9, 14]]) [[44-acts.9.31|Act.9:31 15:3]].
(AS)

4575:
**σεβαστός**, -ή, -όν (σεβάζομαι) 
1. reverend, august. 
2. In late writers, with reference to **the Roman Imperial name**; 
(a) ὁ Σ., Augustus, i.e. the Roman Emperor: [[44-acts.25.21|Act.25:21, 25]]; 
(b) **Augustan**: σπείρα σ., [[44-acts.27.1|Act.27:1]] (See further, Deiss., BS, 218.) 
(AS)

4592:
**σημεῖον**, -ου, τό 
[in LXX chiefly for אוֹת ;] 
**a sign, mark, token**; 
(a) **of that which distinguishes a person or thing from others**: [[40-matthew.26.48|Mat.26:48]] [[42-luke.2.12|Luk.2:12]], [[53-2-thessalonians.3.17|2Th.3:17]] (cf. Deiss., _LAE_, 153.2); before genitive epexeg., [[45-romans.4.11|Rom.4:11;]] with genitive obj., [[40-matthew.24.8|Mat.24:8, 30]], [[47-2-corinthians.12.12|2Co.12:12]]; with genitive subj., [[40-matthew.16.3|Mat.16:3;]] 
